{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 2 Time complexity / Estimating efficiency","source_pages":"27-31","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"complexity","bridge":"complexity_fit","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"先看输入规模，再用时间复杂度估算总操作量。如果两层循环会把规模乘起来，量级很快就会超出时限。","teaching_value":"适合把“先看规模再定方法”讲成学生能落笔估算的一步。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 3 Binary search","source_pages":"41-43","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"binary_search","bridge":"left_bound_update","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"在有序数组里找边界，不是只问“有没有这个值”，而是问“最左边满足条件的位置在哪里”。因此一旦中点已经满足条件，不能急着丢掉它，而要继续保留它作为候选。","teaching_value":"适合解释为什么 a[mid] == x 时还要保留 mid，而不是直接跳到 mid 的右边。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 7 Dynamic programming / Recursive formulation","source_pages":"75-78","topic_l1":"dp","topic_l2":"dp_basic","bridge":"state_design","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"动态规划先要把“一个状态到底在回答什么小问题”说清楚。只有状态含义先站稳，后面才知道这个状态应该依赖哪些更小的状态。","teaching_value":"适合把“状态格里存什么”从代码变量层，拉回子问题语义层。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 7 Dynamic programming / Recursive formulation","source_pages":"76-78","topic_l1":"dp","topic_l2":"dp_basic","bridge":"transition_design","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"先确定当前状态的含义，再看“第一步可以怎么选”或“当前状态能从哪些更小状态转来”。转移式不是凭感觉写出来的，而是由这些更小子问题拼起来的。","teaching_value":"适合解释为什么写转移前要先把来源想全。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Trie structure","source_pages":"254-255","topic_l1":"string","topic_l2":"trie","bridge":"shared_prefix_merging","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"如果很多字符串有相同前缀，它们在 trie 里会先共用一段路径。这样查询时不需要把所有字符串重新逐个看一遍，而是沿当前前缀那条路径往下走。","teaching_value":"适合把“公共前缀为什么值得先合起来看”讲清楚。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Trie structure","source_pages":"254-255","topic_l1":"string","topic_l2":"trie","bridge":"shared_prefix_merging","snippet_type":"algorithm_overview","excerpt":"Trie 的作用不是背答案，而是把字符串集合按前缀组织起来。查询、找最长前缀、统计某个前缀下有多少字符串，都会回到“沿前缀路径走”这件事。","teaching_value":"适合补“这一步在整套方法里负责什么”。","needs_manual_review":false}
